# Item list pagination

Use `@webonone/ui-kit` **`Pagination`** below **`ItemList`** (or equivalent list body) on any page that shows a pageable collection.

Skill: [.cursor/skills/item-list/SKILL.md](../skills/item-list/SKILL.md) — row layout, menus, and detail-page navigation (row click opens details when a details route exists).

## When required

- API returns `total` + `page` + `pageSize` (server pagination)
- Full list loaded once but UI slices by page (client pagination) when row count can grow

## Defaults

| Setting | Value |
|---------|--------|
| Initial `pageSize` state | **12** |
| `pageSizeOptions` (when `onPageSizeChange` is set) | **`[12, 24, 48]`** |

Always initialize `useState(12)` for `pageSize`. Pass `pageSizeOptions={[12, 24, 48]}` so **12** is the default rows-per-page. Server requests must use the same `pageSize` (e.g. `list({ page: 1, pageSize: 12 })`).

## Layout and spacing

```text
FeaturePage                    ← gap-6 between direct children
  filters / tabs (optional)
  ListPageBody                 ← flex-1 column; pagination mt-auto (AppShell + embed fill via ui-kit CSS)
    ItemList                   ← flex-1; current page rows only
    Pagination                 ← mt-auto; sibling below list
```

| Rule | Detail |
|------|--------|
| Sibling order | `ItemList` then `Pagination` inside `ListPageBody` — nothing between them except loading spinner replacing the list |
| Not inside list | Never render `Pagination` inside `ItemList` or between row items |
| List padding | `ItemList` applies **`py-4`** on the `<ul>` via `itemListClassName` — do not strip with `py-0` |
| Bottom alignment | Wrap list + pagination in **`ListPageBody`**; list in **`flex-1`** wrapper; **`Pagination`** gets **`className="mt-auto"`**. AppShell pages: `#main-content` host uses **`flex min-h-full flex-col`**; ui-kit `app-shell-active` CSS fills height — do not add `min-h-0` on `ListPageBody` |
| **WebOnOne iframe embed** | Same markup + **`min-h-full`** flex chain on outlet/`FeaturePage`/`ListPageBody`; scroll on **`PlatformEmbedShell` `<main>`** only — [platform-shell-navigation.mdc](platform-shell-navigation.mdc) |
| Forbidden | Do not place `SearchInput` in the page body on list pages — it belongs in `FeaturePage` `actions` with `ListFilterTrigger` ([list-filter-panel.mdc](list-filter-panel.mdc)); never use plain `Input` for search |
| FeaturePage | Rely on `FeaturePage` `gap-6` between header and body — **do not** add extra `mt-*` on `Pagination` beyond `mt-auto` inside `ListPageBody` |
| Section wrapper | If the list lives in `<section>`, apply `ListPageBody` inside the section for paginated blocks |
| Filters | Filters/tabs stay **above** the list; pagination stays **below** the list |

## Mobile pagination

On viewports below `sm`, `Pagination` renders two rows:

1. **Row 1:** "Showing X–Y of Z" (left) and rows-per-page select (right)
2. **Row 2:** page controls centered

Desktop (`sm+`) keeps a single row: summary left, page size + nav right.

```tsx
{!loading ? (
  <ListPageBody>
    <div className="flex-1">
      <HistoryList items={items} />
    </div>
    <Pagination
      className="mt-auto"
      totalCount={total}
      currentPage={page}
      pageSize={pageSize}
      pageSizeOptions={[12, 24, 48]}
      onPageChange={handlePageChange}
      onPageSizeChange={handlePageSizeChange}
    />
  </ListPageBody>
) : null}
```

## Data loading (Redux epics)

List pages **dispatch load actions** and **select from the feature store** — do not call `apiClient` or feature `*Api` from pages/hooks. See [redux-store-and-epics.mdc](redux-store-and-epics.mdc).

## Server pagination

Parent owns `page`, `pageSize` (default **12**), `total` from store (populated by epic). On filter/tab change → reset `page` to `1` then dispatch load.

```typescript
const [pageSize, setPageSize] = useState(12)

const data = await api.list({ page: nextPage, pageSize, ...filters })
setItems(data.items)
setTotal(data.total)
setPage(data.page)
```

Reference: `email/frontend/src/features/history/pages/HistoryPage.tsx`, `queue/pages/QueuePage.tsx`, `dashboard/pages/DashboardPage.tsx`, `media/.../ScopedFolderBrowser.tsx`.

## Client pagination

Load full array once; slice before passing to list child:

```typescript
const [pageSize, setPageSize] = useState(12)
const visible = items.slice((page - 1) * pageSize, page * pageSize)
```

Reference: `TemplatesPage.tsx`, `CompaniesPage.tsx`, `SystemThemePage.tsx`, `TemplateEditorPage.tsx`.

## Rules

- Import `Pagination` from `@webonone/ui-kit` — no ad-hoc Previous/Next button pairs
- Default **12** rows per page unless a spec documents an exception
- `Pagination` does not fetch — parent handles data and preserves filters on page change
- Use `hideWhenSinglePage` default (`true`) unless product needs visible disabled controls

